      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Where the data comes from**\n\n- Job and step data is the workflow exporter's GitHub job history (SQLite, 60-day retention). A run older than that, or never polled, has no job rows here.\n- Native test data is the JUnit XML inside the run's `osac-logs-[<suite>-]full-install-<run id>` artifact (VMaaS uploads the plain name; BMaaS and CaaS insert the suite), fetched on demand from GitHub and cached for 15 minutes. GitHub keeps workflow artifacts for 7 days; past that the status is `expired` and the counts stay empty, never a green zero.\n- A capture id embeds the GitHub run id and attempt (`<suite>-<prN|main>-<run id>-a<attempt>`, older captures `run-<run id>-attempt-<n>`). A malformed id shows no run at all rather than a guessed one.\n\n**States the native panels can show**\n\n- `unavailable` (a dashboard display state, not a status the endpoint returns): the workflow-exporter endpoint is not deployed or unreachable, so no native evidence was loaded at all. Panels show \"Not deployed or unavailable\" in place of values, a query error, or no content at all (Grafana does not render an error message in panels that loaded after the failed query). See the warning panel at the top.\n- `available`: the JUnit file was parsed; the counts are real.\n- `missing`: no artifact matching the osac-logs full-install pattern exists in the run's repository.\n- `expired`: the artifact passed its 7-day retention.\n- `too_large`: the artifact is above the 64 MiB download bound and was not downloaded.\n- `invalid`: the artifact was downloaded but holds no readable `junit.xml`.\n- `not_requested`: nothing was looked up (no token, a lookup error, or the capture id does not identify a run).\n\n**What this dashboard does not do**\n\n- It shows evidence only. No automatic root-cause diagnosis is generated; the failed-test messages are raw JUnit output.\n- Step durations are the wall-clock time between a step's start and end, not runner minutes.\n- Re-runs overwrite the artifact, so for an older attempt of a re-run run the native results may come from the newest attempt."
      }
    }
